# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Luuk H. E. Kempen et al. (2026). How accurate are foundational machine learning interatomic potentials for heterogeneous catalysis?.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0317672  arXiv:2512.16702v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2512.16702v1 (sha256 97cfdcc6ba52ca5c...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 148 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The paper evaluates 80
# pretrained (foundational) MLIPs zero-shot on catalysis tasks taken from
# published DFT data sets: vacancy formation, adsorbate and
# transition-state formation, reaction, activation and adsorption energies
# and zero-point energies. It trains no MLIP. Read from the arXiv
# preprint (v1).

