###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - All reported errors (MAE/RMSE per model and task, SI Tables S2 onwards) are on derived energies (formation, reaction, activation, adsorption, zero-point), not on total energies, forces or stresses of a test set, so they have no MetricProperty under schema 0.1.2 and were not forced into EnergyProperty. This is the largest per-model evaluation table set met in the corpus (80 models, about a dozen tasks); with derived-property metric individuals it could be encoded against registry models, and SI Table S1 (model family, training data, release) would pin the checkpoints.
# - Target data sets (Table 1): perovskite oxide surfaces (305 vacancy formation energies), reactions on doped zirconia, reactions on metals and single-atom alloys (632 reactions, 1481 adsorbates), metal-oxide nanoclusters (180 zero-point energies), formate on metal-oxide nanoclusters (2869 adsorption energies).
# - The manifest classes the paper as 'Application/model instance'; it is an evaluation study. Read from the arXiv v1 preprint.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
